# Independent reading of the Swagger verification family, written before the stored fields were revealed.
# KEY || independent fields || actor/behavior/trigger/scope/exception/timing/enforcement || entailment test or counterexample
FG-K1-2b15ea3da2 || cls=CD mod=DEFAULT dom=WF rel=PE pol=WF-005~,API-016~,TST-010~,WF-006~ conf=M || actor=agent; act=after an API behavior change verify controllers/tests/metadata, start API on startup or composition change, open Development Swagger UI and confirm it loads, exercise endpoints when meaningful, preserve behavior in tests; trig=API behavior changes (outer when-clause); scope=swagger knowledge skill, on invocation; exc=none stated; time=post-change verification, before completion; enf=instruction text only || test=Counterexample: a controller status code changes; build, integration tests and OpenAPI JSON checks pass; no startup or composition change; agent never opens the UI. WF-005, API-016, TST-010 satisfied and WF-006 not triggered, yet the literal step is unperformed. The UI step carries no when-clause of its own, so the outer trigger governs it. Not entailed.
FG-K1-358e1806b9 || cls=CO mod=DEFAULT dom=WF rel=FE pol=WF-006 conf=M || actor=agent; act=verify Development startup, as applicable: host, endpoint, Swagger UI when API exposes it, config binding, DB, frontend, API base URL and CORS; trig=new runnable application or substantial composition/startup/config/persistence/full-stack change; scope=verify skill; exc=as applicable, Swagger UI only when exposed; time=runtime smoke before completion; enf=text || test=Source says Default. Trigger and strength match WF-006. The list instantiates key composition surfaces under an as-applicable hedge. Residual: an agent could read WF-006 as met without the UI, so the enumeration is an instantiation rather than strict logical entailment.
FG-M-268251a6d0 || cls=XW mod=DEFAULT dom=WF rel=NE pol=- conf=M || actor=agent; act=open Development Swagger UI and confirm it loads; exercise representative endpoints through Swagger when meaningful; trig=API behavior changes; step 5 additionally when a meaningful behavioral check; scope=swagger skill; exc=none; time=post-change; enf=text || test=Numbered step 4 is its own list item with no condition, so it reaches every API behavior change. Counterexample as for K1: tests and metadata pass, no UI opened. No canonical policy requires it.
FG-M-fd05eef14c || cls=CO mod=DEFAULT dom=WF rel=FE pol=WF-005~,API-016~,WF-006~ conf=M || actor=agent; act=verify Controller behavior and integration tests, response metadata, start API when startup or composition affected; trig=API behavior changes; scope=swagger skill; exc=none; time=post-change; enf=text || test=Steps 1-3 restate duties in WF-005, API-016 and WF-006. Note the start step fires on any startup or composition effect whereas WF-006 says substantial; that small trigger difference is not resolved by text.
FG-M-0dcdca28e3 || cls=CO mod=DEFAULT dom=WF rel=FE pol=WF-006 conf=M || actor=agent; act=verify startup with intended Development configuration; as applicable API host, endpoint, Swagger UI, config, DB, frontend, CORS; build alone is not proof; trig=new runnable app or substantial composition/startup/config/persistence/full-stack change; scope=verify skill workflow; exc=as applicable; time=before completion; enf=text || test=Same trigger as WF-006. Stated without Default marker, workflow-skill step. Instantiates key composition surfaces. Modality could be read MUST as a workflow step, but WF-006 itself is DEFAULT and the runtime text has no must.
FG-M-37676d6579 || cls=CO mod=MUST dom=WF rel=FE pol=TST-010 conf=H || actor=agent; act=represent behavior uniquely shown by ad-hoc probe in maintained automated tests; trig=ad-hoc or manual probe uniquely demonstrated behavior; scope=verify, testing, code-review, build-fix; exc=equivalent coverage already exists; time=before completion; enf=text || test=Restates TST-010 including its exception. Builds and existing runs not requiring tests is a clarification implied by the probe trigger. The confirm-existing-test wording adds nothing falsifiable beyond equivalent coverage.
FG-M1-a876ee45ce || cls=XW mod=DEFAULT dom=WF rel=NE pol=- conf=M || actor=agent; act=open Development Swagger UI and confirm it loads; trig=API behavior changes; scope=swagger skill; exc=none; time=post-change; enf=text || test=Run-in series whose conditional items each carry their own when-clause (start when, exercise when); the UI item carries none, so grammar attaches only the outer trigger. Alternative sequence reading (start then open) is weaker because it needs a condition the text attaches to a different comma item. Counterexample as for K1.
FG-M1-51dccbe9d9 || cls=CD mod=DEFAULT dom=WF rel=PE pol=WF-005~,API-016~,WF-006~ conf=M || actor=agent; act=verify Controller/tests, metadata; start API when startup or composition changed; confirm UI loads; exercise endpoints when meaningful; trig=API behavior changes; scope=swagger skill; exc=none; time=post-change; enf=text || test=Compound. Canonical part as in K1. Remainder: UI confirmation and meaningful endpoint exercise, not entailed. The claim text joins start-and-confirm-UI with and, but the source separates them by comma as parallel items.
FG-M1-b95ccac9b7 || cls=CO mod=DEFAULT dom=WF rel=FE pol=WF-006 conf=M || actor=agent; act=verify intended Development startup and key composition surfaces as applicable, including Swagger UI reachable when expected; trig=new runnable application or substantial change; scope=verify skill; exc=as applicable; time=before completion; enf=text || test=Same trigger and object as WF-006. Swagger evidence range at swagger skill 117-122 is a different trigger and does not belong to this claim.
FG-M1-ae7b6c7526 || cls=CO mod=DEFAULT dom=WF rel=FE pol=WF-006 conf=M || actor=agent; act=verify Development startup and key composition surfaces; trig=new runnable or substantial; scope=verify skill; exc=as applicable; time=before completion; enf=text || test=Direct restatement of WF-006.
FG-M1-e0f9cd2b5b || cls=CO mod=DEFAULT dom=WF rel=FE pol=TST-010~ conf=M || actor=agent; act=preserve newly verified behavior as maintained tests per verify section; trig=API behavior changes; scope=swagger skill; exc=by reference, equivalent coverage; time=before completion; enf=text || test=Cross-reference to verify imports TST-010 with its exception; no independent duty. Weaker in form because it sits in a knowledge skill.
FG-M1-fd434c3072 || cls=CO mod=MUST dom=WF rel=FE pol=TST-010 conf=H || actor=agent; act=probe that establishes behavior is preserved before removal; builds need no new tests; trig=probe established or uniquely demonstrated behavior; scope=build-fix, verify, testing, code-review; exc=equivalent coverage exists; time=before completion and before probe removal; enf=text || test=Restates TST-010. Before-removal timing follows from preserving before completion.
FG-L0-084aeff176 || cls=XW mod=DEFAULT dom=WF rel=NE pol=- conf=M || actor=agent; act=open the Development Swagger UI; trig=API changes (section heading: Verification after API changes); scope=swagger skill; exc=none; time=post-change; enf=text || test=No confirm-it-loads wording here, only open. Heading says API changes, broader than behavior changes. Run-in sentence; the following when-clause has its own subject (that is a meaningful check refers to exercising). Counterexample as for K1: metadata and tests pass, UI not opened.
FG-L0-ad2b418693 || cls=CD mod=DEFAULT dom=WF rel=PE pol=WF-005~,API-016~,WF-006~ conf=M || actor=agent; act=verify controller, integration tests, metadata; start API when startup or composition changed; open UI; exercise when meaningful; trig=API changes; scope=swagger skill; exc=none; time=post-change; enf=text || test=Compound with the same remainder as K1, but open-only, no confirm-it-loads.
FG-L0-1fbbe47cb4 || cls=CO mod=DEFAULT dom=WF rel=FE pol=WF-006 conf=H || actor=agent; act=verify intended Development startup and key composition surfaces as applicable; trig=new runnable or substantial; scope=verify skill; exc=as applicable; time=before completion; enf=text || test=Almost verbatim WF-006.
FG-L0-3ed43fa3b6 || cls=CO mod=DEFAULT dom=WF rel=FE pol=WF-006 conf=M || actor=agent; act=same smoke list; trig=new runnable or substantial; scope=verify skill; exc=as applicable; time=before completion; enf=text || test=Enumerated surfaces, as applicable. Swagger skill range is a different trigger.
FG-L0-6891070daf || cls=CO mod=MUST dom=WF rel=FE pol=TST-010 conf=H || actor=agent; act=preserve behavior from temporary probe; trig=probe uniquely verified behavior; scope=build-fix, verify, testing, code-review; exc=equivalent coverage; time=before completion; enf=text || test=Restates TST-010.
FG-L1-de692b7c3d || cls=XW mod=DEFAULT dom=WF rel=NE pol=- conf=M || actor=agent; act=open Development Swagger UI; exercise representative endpoints when meaningful; trig=API behavior changes; scope=swagger skill; exc=none; time=post-change; enf=text || test=Same structure as L0, with API behavior changes as outer trigger. Open-only. Exercise carries when meaningful. Counterexample as for K1.
FG-L1-a48ca2a20d || cls=CD mod=DEFAULT dom=WF rel=PE pol=WF-005~,API-016~,WF-006~ conf=M || actor=agent; act=verify controller, tests, metadata; start when startup changed; open UI; exercise when meaningful; trig=API behavior changes; scope=swagger skill; exc=none; time=post-change; enf=text || test=Compound with the same remainder.
FG-L1-32700af18e || cls=CD mod=DEFAULT dom=WF rel=PE pol=WF-006~ conf=M || actor=agent; act=apply migrations explicitly to a local Development DB, start API, confirm seeder populates empty DB or leaves existing unchanged; trig=persistence capability workflow change; scope=ef-core capability workflow; exc=none; time=verification section; enf=text || test=WF-006 covers startup verification but does not require applying migrations locally and watching the seeder. Agent running the app against an already migrated DB satisfies WF-006 but not this step. Swagger and verify ranges support only the general smoke part.
FG-L1-8ab7d71dd3 || cls=CO mod=DEFAULT dom=WF rel=FE pol=TST-010~ conf=M || actor=agent; act=preserve newly verified behavior as tests per verify step 4; trig=API behavior changes; scope=swagger skill; exc=by reference; time=before completion; enf=text || test=Cross-reference imports TST-010.
FG-L1-ad6351ae73 || cls=CO mod=MUST dom=WF rel=FE pol=TST-010 conf=H || actor=agent; act=behavioral probe follows verify step 4; builds need no new tests; trig=probe establishes behavior; scope=build-fix, testing, code-review; exc=equivalent coverage; time=before completion; enf=text || test=Restates TST-010 by reference.
FG-K0-47988fe869 || cls=XW mod=DEFAULT dom=WF rel=NE pol=- conf=H || actor=agent; act=open Development Swagger UI and confirm it loads; trig=API changes (section heading); scope=swagger skill; exc=none; time=post-change; enf=text || test=Numbered step 5 is its own item with no condition; step 4's when-clause is grammatically confined to step 4. So no reach ambiguity in K0. Counterexample as for K1.
FG-K0-9522259b92 || cls=CD mod=DEFAULT dom=WF rel=PE pol=WF-005~,API-016~,TST-010~,WF-006~ conf=M || actor=agent; act=numbered list: verify Controller, tests, metadata; start when startup or composition affected; open UI and confirm; exercise when meaningful and preserve; trig=API changes; scope=swagger skill; exc=none; time=post-change; enf=text || test=Compound with the same remainder.
FG-K0-95583b3fcb || cls=CO mod=DEFAULT dom=WF rel=FE pol=WF-006 conf=M || actor=agent; act=verify local Development startup as applicable, including Swagger UI loads when API exposes it; trig=new runnable or substantial; scope=verify skill; exc=as applicable; time=before completion; enf=text || test=Source says Default. Instantiation of key composition surfaces.
